@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+---
+id: task-001-implement-rfc-6901-json-pointer-resolvepointer
+type: task
+title: "Implement RFC 6901 JSON Pointer resolvePointer"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) and export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+It must return the value a pointer refers to, and throw when the pointer is syntactically invalid or
+does not resolve to a value in the document. First of a series of features that build on each other.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Wrote `src/index.test.ts` first (red), covering the RFC 6901 §5 worked example (including every
+  escaped-character case: `~0`, `~1`, and the members that need no escaping), plus error paths:
+  malformed escape, pointer not starting with `/`, missing member, non-numeric array index, leading-zero
+  array index, out-of-bounds array index, descending into a scalar, and a non-string pointer. Confirmed
+  the suite failed with the module missing.
+- Implemented `src/index.ts` (green): exports `JsonValue` (recursive JSON value type) and
+  `resolvePointer`. Splits the pointer into tokens on `/`, unescapes `~1` before `~0` (decode order
+  matters, otherwise `~01` corrupts), validates each array token against the RFC's `array-index` ABNF
+  (`0` or a non-zero-leading digit sequence), and walks the document token by token, throwing a plain
+  `Error` on any invalid syntax or unresolved path.
+- `npm test` (Node's native TS execution): 14/14 passing, 100% line/branch/function coverage
+  (`--experimental-test-coverage`).
+- Added `typescript` and `@types/node` as devDependencies (none existed; `tsc --noEmit` could not even
+  run), and `typecheck`/`build` scripts. Extended `tsconfig.json` with `types: ["node"]`,
+  `rewriteRelativeImportExtensions: true` and `rootDir: "src"` so the same `.ts`-extension relative
+  imports that Node's native TS execution requires also satisfy `tsc`'s module resolution, while
+  `tsc`'s build output still rewrites them to `.js`. `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` both pass
+  cleanly on the new code.
+
+## Follow-up for later features
+
+`JsonValue` is exported from `src/index.ts` for reuse by the pointer-based features planned next
+(get/set/patch-style operations), so they share one JSON value type instead of redefining it.
